    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d490-a1">

                <pb facs="0845" n="751" xml:id="pg751"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 253.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mariscal to Mr. Connery.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-10-19"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 19,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chargé d’affaires</hi>: I have the honor to
                    acknowledge the receipt of your note, dated yesterday, in which you are pleased
                    to inform me that the honorable Secretary of State of the United States has read
                    with satisfaction the report that you sent to him respecting our last
                    conversation about the relations between Mexico and Guatemala.</p>
                <p>In reply, it is pleasing to me to inform you that I appreciate fully the fact
                    that the honorable Mr. Bayard does justice to the frankness and sincerity with
                    which Mexico expresses her sentiments in no way hostile toward Guatemala.</p>
                <p>I protest to you, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Igno. Mariscal.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
